                <pb facs="0289" n="257" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v19/pg257"/>

                <head>119. Telegram From the Embassy in Poland to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d119-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Warsaw</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-09-22T17:00:00+02:00">September 22,
                            1958, 5 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>453. USUN For Robertson. Beam-Wang Talks.
                        Wang presented at today’s meeting following draft
                    agreed announcement.</p>
                <p>Draft agreed announcement of Governments of PRC
                    and USA on easing and eliminating tension in Taiwan Straits area.</p>
                <p>In order ease and eliminate tension in Taiwan Straits area and help safeguard
                    peace in Far East and world, Ambassador Wang
                        Ping-nan, on behalf of Government of PRC and Ambassador Jacob D.
                        Beam, on behalf of Government of USA, agree to announce: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Government of PRC and Government of
                            USA undertake jointly, without prejudice to principles of mutual respect
                            for territorial integrity and sovereignty and non-interference in each
                            others internal affairs, to settle disputes between the two countries in
                            Taiwan area and other areas in Far East through peaceful negotiations
                            without resorting to threat or use of force against each other.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Government of USA declares that, in order eliminate provocations, it
                            undertakes withdraw all its armed forces from Taiwan, Penghu Islands and
                            Taiwan Straits area.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Ambassadors of the two countries will continue their talks on specific
                            matters concerning above two paragraphs of present agreed
                            announcement.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Beam</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
